{
  "dom_id": "step-q337208",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "A jar has $6$ chips labeled with one, $4$ chips labeled with four, $3$ chips labeled with nine, and $2$ chips labeled with twelve. If one chip is randomly drawn from the jar,  what is its expected value? Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\text{E}[X]=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value labeled on a randomly drawn chip. Then the support is $S={1,4,9,12}.$\n\nIn the jar, there are $6$ chips labeled with one, $4$ chips labeled with four, $3$ chips labeled with nine, and $2$ chips labeled with twelve (fifteen chips in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1) & =\\frac{6}{15}=\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ P(4) & =\\frac{4}{15} \\\\ P(9) & =\\frac{3}{15}=\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ P(12) & =\\frac{2}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+4\\cdot f(4)+9\\cdot f(9)+12\\cdot f(12) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{2}{5})+4(\\frac{4}{15})+9(\\frac{1}{5})+12(\\frac{2}{15}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{16}{15}+\\frac{9}{5}+\\frac{24}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{15}+\\frac{16}{15}+\\frac{27}{15}+\\frac{24}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+16+27+24}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{73}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
